		{
			dependencies: ["7DBC7E2955637282"]
			description: [
				"Encased chain drives may be placed side by side either vertically or horizontally to form a chain passing rotational power among all the blocks. The blocks must touch on their sides (not axis to side) and be in a single straight line to form a chain."
				""
				"The axes of the encased chain drives may be all parallel or blocks can be rotated to orient the axis perpendicularly. Encased chain drives can also pass rotational power through their rotating axis, but this is not a continuation of the same chain."
			]
			id: "074E60C5E08AC196"
			tasks: [{
				id: "546317F9E98CA005"
				item: "create:encased_chain_drive"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 5.5d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7DBC7E2955637282"]
			description: [
				"The Chain Conveyor is used to transport Cardboard Packages. It has a secondary use of transferring rotational force across open spaces."
				""
				"After placing a Chain Conveyor, they can be connected to other Chain Conveyors by right-clicking them with a Chain. The selection can be cleared by right-clicking the Chain Conveyor again. The maximum distance at which chain conveyors can be connected is 32 blocks."
				""
				"Right-click a Chain Conveyor with a Wrench to take a ride. Sneak to dismount. When approaching an intersection, the player will be sent in the direction they’re looking towards"
				""
				"Cardboard Packages can be placed on Chain Conveyors via right-click. Package Frogports are used to automatically move Cardboard Packages from and to the Chain Conveyors. Chain Conveyors will automatically sort packages by their Address to send them to Frogports with a matching Address."
			]
			id: "5210BFF097EA8975"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5A043FC1B4A816F7"
				item: "create:chain_conveyor"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 9.5d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7DBC7E2955637282"]
			description: [
				"The Cuckoo Clock is powered by connecting a Shaft, or other rotational component, to the back of the clock."
				""
				"The Cuckoo Clock can run at any rotational speed, and produces stress equivalent to it's speed."
				""
				"Besides showing the in-game time, the Cuckoo Clock also chimes twice daily, once at noon, and once dusk (as soon as players can sleep). At noon a small pig pops in and out of the clock 3 times and makes an oinking sounds, at dusk a small creeper pops in and out of the clock 3 times and makes hissing sounds."
			]
			id: "23F98B0601B33966"
			tasks: [{
				id: "49A0715BB5AB1645"
				item: "create:cuckoo_clock"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 4.5d
			y: 1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7DBC7E2955637282"]
			description: [
				"The Millstone is a more basic equivalent to the Crushing Wheels, and is most likely the first of the two that the Player will construct. It is capable of applying milling recipes to any valid items inserted from above or from the sides with use of any instering block (funnel, pipes, etc.). "
				""
				"Unlike many create contraptions, millstones are capable of receiving rotational force from both cogs (from the side) and shafts (from the bottom)."
			]
			id: "799038DEE9B54AF9"
			tasks: [{
				id: "58E5EE19C2A582E6"
				item: "create:millstone"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 4.5d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7DBC7E2955637282"]
			description: [
				"The Mechanical Press is a mechanical component that applies Pressing, Packing, and Compacting recipes to items below it. It is an important early-game item, as it is used to press Ingots into Sheets, which are important ingredients for higher-level components."
				""
				"The Mechanical Press is powered by an internal Shaft, accessed from two opposite sides. Much like Shafts, Presses will relay rotation along their axis. It processes items faster when it receives faster rotational power."
				""
				"By default, the Mechanical Press will apply Pressing recipes to items underneath it. When a Mechanical Press is placed above a Basin, it will apply Packing or Compacting recipes to ingredients in the Basin."
			]
			id: "7F1FC387AB804DD8"
			rewards: [{
				count: 4
				id: "411BEB7E5F92DAF5"
				item: "create:andesite_casing"
				type: "item"
			}]
			size: 1.5d
			tasks: [{
				id: "658BA4382782FD89"
				item: "create:mechanical_press"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 12.5d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7DBC7E2955637282"]
			description: [
				"The Depot is used as an interaction point for machines."
				""
				"Items can be right clicked or inserted onto the depot. Machines such as Mechanical Presses will interact with the items the same way they would on a Mechanical Belt. Items on a depot will not despawn, and will stay there until they are extracted by a player or another machin"
			]
			id: "2645642809E498BB"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5BE710DD854A06C5"
				item: "create:depot"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 5.5d
			y: -4.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7DBC7E2955637282"]
			description: [
				"The Speedometer measures the speed of Rotational Force."
				""
				"When connected to a component, the speed of the rotation is shown by a hand on the face of the Speedometer. The higher the hand is, the faster the rotation. "
				""
				"The Stressometer is used to measure the amount of Stress on a Shaft. This stress is the \"load\" of the system."
				""
				"When connected to a component, the amount of stress in the system versus the stress capacity is shown by a hand on the face of the Stressometer. The higher the hand is, the more stress there is in the system. It can also output a Redstone Comparator signal, outputting at a strength of 15 when the system is overstressed."
			]
			icon: "create:speedometer"
			id: "16DC5CDD7C89F395"
			min_required_tasks: 1
			shape: "hexagon"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "24F9B33762C0D103"
					item: "create:speedometer"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "69F9FC661DBED057"
					item: "create:stressometer"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			x: 8.5d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7DBC7E2955637282"]
			description: [
				"The Mechanical Piston is a piston that can push Contraptions when powered with Rotational Power."
				""
				"To extend, the Piston must have Piston Extension Poles at the end as well as Rotational power. The maximum extension pole length is 64 blocks."
				""
				"When the rotation is reversed, the piston will retract. The end must be made sticky with a Slimeball to bring the pushed blocks back with it."
				""
				"A placed Mechanical Piston can be made sticky by right-clicking it with a Slimeball."
				""
				"Multiple blocks can be pushed with the use of Chassis."
			]
